hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1009","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Iyad Abdullah al-Qurashi and others told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id. Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you prays, let him put on his shoes, or take them off between his legs, and he should not harm anyone else with them.”"
"1010","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, Abu Salamah told us, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Ya’qub also narrated to us, Ibn Ulayya narrated to us, Sa’id bin Yazid, who is Abu Maslamah, narrated to us, h and he narrated to us Bundar, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I said to Anas bin Malik: Was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Does he pray in sandals? He said: Yes.”"
"1011","Al-Fadl bin Sahl narrated to us, Othman bin Omar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He was praying over the wine room and said: “O Aisha, remove this mat of yours from us, for I feared it would tempt people.”"
"1012","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us strange news. Ibn Wahb told us. Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: I keep hearing that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed over a wine bottle,” and he said: On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray over wine and prostrate over it.”"
"1013","This is Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami, I am Mu’alla bin Mansour, Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would pray over wine, and would not leave it while he was traveling or at home.” This is how Al-Makhramī narrated it with a chain of transmission traceable back to us. If it was preserved in this chain of transmission and was narrated as a chain of transmission, then this is strange news, and so is the report of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Anas Gharib"
